  "ref": "EZK.42.20",
  "review_notes": [
    "בֵּין הַקֹּדֶשׁ לְחֹל is read by the connective the ASV actually writes (rule 26): בֵּין takes *between* and the לְ takes *and*.",
    "The possessive חוֹמָה לוֹ clause is verbless, so the לְ carries *had* and its suffix the subject pronoun (rule 43).",
    "The two substantival expressions differ by whether an article morpheme is present: הַקֹּדֶשׁ takes *that which* on its article (rule 41), while anarthrous חֹל takes it into its own unit and heads on *common* (rule 46)."
  ]
